  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Npc133119 may be associated with Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 through multiple indirect pathways. The first path links Npc133119 to Natural resistance-associated macrophage protein 2, which in turn targets Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2. The second path connects Npc133119 to ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3, which targets Isorhamnetin 3-robinobioside, which also targets the same enzyme. The third path links Npc133119 to Induced myeloid leukemia cell differentiation protein Mcl-1, which targets Firategrast, which again targets the enzyme. These pathways collectively indicate that Npc133119 may influence the activity of Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving signaling or regulatory interactions. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear, as the evidence is indirect and spans multiple layers of molecular regulation.",
